    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="1096" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v15/pg1064"/>

                <head>511. Telegram From the Embassy in Thailand to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d511-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1959-01-29T12:00:00+07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                                1959—noon.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1891. [<hi rendition="#italic">2 paragraphs (11½ lines of source text) not
                        declassified</hi>]</p>
                <pb facs="1097" n="1065" xml:id="pg1065"/>
                <p>King still intensely interested in paying State visit to US in Spring 1960.</p>
                <p>Foregoing conversation took place during USIS
                    function opening Lincoln Sesquicentennial attended by King last night.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
